        "original_id": "81742161-c990-5ff4-9587-df3ef14f92a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elizabeth Smylie, Liz Smylie, Vasek Pospisil, Jack Sock, Nicole Provis, Jo-Anne Faull, Julie Richardson\n- Events: 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles, 2014 Wimbledon Championships, 2015 Indian Wells Masters, 1994 ATP Tour\n- Organizations: ATP, International Tennis Federation\n- Concepts: Grand Slam titles, women's doubles, mixed doubles, defending champions\n\nFacts:\n- Elizabeth Smylie, née Sayers and sometimes known as Liz Smylie, was born on 11 April 1963 and is a retired Australian professional tennis player.\n- Elizabeth Smylie won four Grand Slam titles during her career: one in women's doubles and three in mixed doubles.\n- In the 1992 Dow Classic – Doubles, defending champions Nicole Provis and Elizabeth Smylie lost in the quarterfinals to Jo-Anne Faull and Julie Richardson.\n- In 1994, the ATP Tour included the Grand Slam tournaments, the ATP Championship Series, Single-Week, the ATP World Series, the ATP World Team Cup, the Davis Cup, the ATP Tour World Championships, and the Grand Slam Cup.\n- In the 1994 ATP Tour structure, the International Tennis Federation organized the Grand Slam tournaments, the Davis Cup, and the Grand Slam Cup.\n- Vasek Pospisil and Jack Sock won the men's doubles titles at the 2014 Wimbledon Championships and the 2015 Indian Wells Masters.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
